  <div class="about-page">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      <em>Bedroom Dialectics</em> is where I write down things I'm trying to understand.
    </p>

    <p>
      Most of it comes from paying attention to the friction beneath everyday life: the physical machinery that keeps modern civilization from collapsing, the quiet habits we repeat without questioning, and the gap between clean abstractions and the messy reality of living inside them.
    </p>

    <p>
      When thoughts stay trapped in your head, they tend to feel either deceptively simple or impossibly heavy. Writing them down into sentences—late at night, without an audience to perform for—is just a way to test what actually holds weight and what dissolves under honest scrutiny.
    </p>

    <p>
      No grand theories or prepackaged conclusions. Just an ongoing attempt to look closely at ordinary things and think through them with whatever clarity is available.
    </p>

